  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ICAR operations 2021-2024</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Aim of the support: Through Basel Institute on Governance provide Support to International Center for Asset Recovery (ICAR) for implementation of Operational Strategy 2021-2024 for  global and national efforts to prevent and  fight corruption, money laundering, Assist developing countries in the prevention of corruption and financial crime and provide technical assistance and advice to recover stolen assets.  Develpment of knowledge products, participation in the global discurse and policy making. Training and capacity building of national actors (public prosecution, police, anti-corruption agencies, financial intelligence units and other.  

Impact: &quot;ICAR partner countries are more successful in deterring corruption and mobilising resources for development and can rely on greater public trust in government bacause they are effective in recovering stollen assets.&quot;

Outcomes: 
1) ICAR partner countries have anti-corruption chains that are better equipped to deliver sanctions and recover assets, 
2) ICAR contributes to the development of stronger laws and international standards to make asset recovery more efficient

Partner countries are: Malawi, Mozambique, Tanzania/Zanzibar, Zambia, Sao Tome e Principe, Seychelles, Colombia, Peru, Ukraine and Zimbabwe.</narrative>
  </description>
